.TH UMOUNT 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
umount \- unmount filesystems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B umount
.IR dir ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B umount
takes away the filesystem mounted at each
.I dir
named. A failure is reported on standard error as
.BI "umount: " dir ": " reason
and the rest are still tried.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every one was unmounted (or none was named), 1 if any could not be.
.SH NOTES
Only a mount point is taken, not a device, and there are no options.
The kernel mounts and unmounts the bus's disks by itself as they come
and go.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mount (1),
.BR df (1)
